{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "4e56f716-0b20-44a7-b716-b8bd60decb89",
    "name": "Adesua - Member C (learning, enrollments, orders, instructor stats)",
    "description": "Requests for every endpoint Member C owns, matching docs/API_CONTRACT.md. Each request has saved example responses (success and errors) under it.\n\nEnvironments\nUse the environment files in docs/postman/:\n- Adesua local (`adesua-local.postman_environment.json`): the backend on your computer.\n- Adesua production (`adesua-production.postman_environment.json`): the live API on Render (see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md). The first request after a quiet period can take up to a minute. Requests that enroll, buy or complete lessons change the live data.\n\nHow to use\n1. Import this file and the environment you need, then choose that environment (top right).\n2. Run Auth > Log in as student first. It saves the token as `{{token}}`, and the other requests send it automatically.\n3. Open this collection's Variables tab and set `freeCourseId` and `paidCourseId` to the `_id` of a free and a paid published course (GET /api/courses lists them).\n4. Run Enroll in a free course, then Course lessons. It saves the first lesson's `_id` as `{{lessonId}}` for Mark a lesson complete.\n5. Run Start checkout. It saves the order's `_id` as `{{orderId}}` for Pay an order.\n6. Run Auth > Log in as instructor before Instructor stats, and Log in as student again before the student requests.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
